@tarekgh Thanks! I can provide the implementation if neccesary. 

In our own code we already implement the proposed methods simply by falling back on the original DateTime methods after conversion.
For example:

```csharp
public static int GetWeekOfYear(DateOnly date)
{
    var dt = date.ToDateTime(TimeOnly.MinValue, DateTimeKind.Unspecified);
    return GetWeekOfYear(dt);
}
```

If that is okay, I can open a PR with these implementations whenever ready.

Implementing this the other way around (e.g. making the DateOnly methods the base implementation and rewriting the existing DateTime methods to be the overload/conversion), is possible too but is a slightly larger change.
